[00:25.26] Eyeless in the morning sun, you were
[00:28.90] Pale and mild, a modern girl
[00:32.60] Taken with thought, still prone to care
[00:36.42] Making tea in your underwear
[00:39.64] You went out in the yard to find
[00:46.28] Something to eat and clear your mind
[00:51.48] Something bad inside me went away
[01:02.96] Quaking leaves and broken light
[01:06.14] Shifting skin, the coming night
[01:10.28] The bearers of all good things arrive
[01:14.16] Climb inside us, twist and cry
[01:17.74] A kiss on your molten eyes
[01:23.58] Myriad lives like blades of grass
[01:29.24] Yet to be realized
[01:31.58] Bow as they pass
[01:40.13] They are cold
[01:42.17] Still
[01:44.47] Waiting in the ether to form
[01:49.73] Feel
[01:51.65] Kill
[01:53.73] Propagate only to die
[02:42.47] They are cold
[02:44.33] Still
[02:46.53] Waiting in the ether to form
[02:52.37] Feel
[02:54.05] Kill
[02:56.19] Propagate only to die
[03:01.63] Dissolve
[03:03.89] Magically, absurdly
[03:07.11] They'll end
[03:09.25] Leave
[03:11.53] Dissipate coldly
[03:14.67] And strangely return
